From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <github@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] WebOSSurfaceItem::close: ask xdg clients to close
 themselves

0012 made close() kill the wl_client when an item has no webOS shell
surface, so that SDL apps could be dismissed at all. Since 0016 advertises
xdg_wm_base those clients now have a shell role, and xdg_toplevel.close is
both the protocol's way to ask and the only one that lets the client tear
its own window down.

It matters for more than tidiness. Waydroid's hwcomposer handles
xdg_toplevel.close by dropping the Android task, setting
waydroid.active_apps to none and erasing the window. Killing its wl_client
instead takes down the connection SurfaceFlinger composites through, and
Android rebuilds it - so swiping the Waydroid card away brought it straight
back instead of closing it.

Keep the client-close as the last resort, for clients that have neither a
webOS shell surface nor an xdg_toplevel.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/modules/weboscompositor/weboscorecompositor.cpp
+++ b/modules/weboscompositor/weboscorecompositor.cpp
@@ -283,6 +283,15 @@
         qInfo() << "xdg_toplevel created" << toplevel << "configuring fullscreen" << size;
         toplevel->sendFullscreen(size);
 
+        /* Remember the toplevel on the item so WebOSSurfaceItem::close() can
+         * send xdg_toplevel.close instead of killing the whole client. Stored
+         * as a dynamic property to keep this out of the item's public header.
+         */
+        if (xdgSurface && xdgSurface->surface()) {
+            if (WebOSSurfaceItem *item = WebOSSurfaceItem::getSurfaceItemFromSurface(xdgSurface->surface()))
+                item->setProperty("_luneosXdgToplevel", QVariant::fromValue<QObject *>(toplevel));
+        }
+
         /* Carry appId across to the surface item. wl_webos_shell clients set it
          * through WebOSShellSurface; xdg_shell clients set xdg_toplevel.app_id,
          * and without this the item has no identity for the card shell to use.
--- a/modules/weboscompositor/webossurfaceitem.cpp
+++ b/modules/weboscompositor/webossurfaceitem.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include <QQmlEngine>
 #include <QOpenGLTexture>
 #include <QDebug>
+#include <QWaylandXdgShell>
 
 #include <qweboskeyextension.h>
 
@@ -1107,6 +1108,18 @@
     if (m_shellSurface) {
         sendCloseToGroupItems();
         m_shellSurface->close();
+    } else if (QWaylandXdgToplevel *toplevel =
+                   qobject_cast<QWaylandXdgToplevel *>(property("_luneosXdgToplevel").value<QObject *>())) {
+        /* An xdg_shell client has a proper way to be asked to go away, and it
+         * is the only one that lets the client tear the window down itself.
+         * Waydroid's hwcomposer, for one, uses xdg_toplevel.close to drop the
+         * Android task and clear waydroid.active_apps; killing its wl_client
+         * instead takes down the connection SurfaceFlinger composites through,
+         * which Android simply rebuilds - so a swiped-away card came straight
+         * back. Only fall through to closing the client when there is neither
+         * a webOS shell surface nor an xdg_toplevel.
+         */
+        toplevel->sendClose();
     } else {
         qWarning() << "No webos shell surface exist, will close entire client !";
         if (surface() && surface()->client()) {
